@@ -0,0 +1,23 @@
+---
+type: decision
+status: active
+updated: 2026-11-03
+sources: [.harness/gate-shrink-detail.md, .harness/spike-bprime/RESULTS.md, 0005, 0011, commit de13cf2, commit 5a950ed]
+verified_by: tests/gate.test.sh + tests/gate-denied.list
+---
+# 0012: Gate shrink: keep a trimmed gate, not permissions rules
+
+**Context.** The "4b" item of the 0005 consequences asked to replace the 529-line gate with `permissions` rules plus a ~50-line gate. The analyst measured the gate (552 lines, `.harness/gate-shrink-detail.md` §2) and replayed 881 conductor Bash calls from 8 transcripts through it: 754 allowed, 127 denied (§3; 106 of the denies came from two sessions that ran ungated). Never used in those 754: `git show --stat`, `herdr status`, `pane list|layout`, `workspace|tab list`, `gh issue|run|repo|auth|browse|pr status`, jq as a pipe consumer. 44 allowed calls (5.8%) chained with an unquoted `;` or `&`; none used a pipe or `2>&1`. The B′ spike (native subagents replacing the harness runner) was rejected on 2026-11-03 (`.harness/spike-bprime/RESULTS.md`): subagents die when the conductor exits ("1 local agent couldn't be moved and was stopped"), so the runner and therefore the gate stay.
+
+**Decision.** Keep the gate and trim it by the plan in §7, done across earlier steps and this one:
+- keyed on hook `agent_type` (closes the daemon-inherits-worker-env hole), `tests/gate-denied.list` as the regression list, one-command scanner (wiki: conductor-shell-one-command), already shipped before step 5;
+- allowlist limited to `harness`, `gh pr create|view|list|checks|comment|edit|merge` (`--body-file` only under `.harness/`/`docs/`, no `merge -d`, no `api`), `herdr pane get|current`, `git status|log|diff --stat|branch` (list-only regex), `cat`/`ls` under `.harness/` and `docs/`; no jq, `git show`, other herdr verbs;
+- native subagent tools come off through `disallowedTools` in `claude/agents/conductor.md` (Agent, Workflow, Monitor, NotebookEdit), not gate cases; the hook MATCHER is `Edit|Write|Read|Grep|Glob|Bash`; there is no filesystem MCP server configured, so no `mcp__filesystem__*` block;
+- policy tables (BASH_ALLOW, GH_ALLOW, GIT_DENY, deny messages) sit in one labelled block at the top (commit 2 of step 5); every "You may run directly" form in conductor.md has a gate test.
+- Kept: the path helpers (`rel`, `physrel`, `physical`, readable/writable, raw-stream deny, ~109 lines) and the Bash character allowlist. They are the symlink, `..` and raw-stream (0007) protection and cannot shrink without losing it.
+- Rejected, option f (replace with `permissions` rules): user-scope rules bind workers too (same settings file), deny beats allow so "deny Read except `.harness/` and `docs/`" cannot be written, and Bash patterns are fragile. Only tool-name denies are expressible, which `disallowedTools` already covers.
+- Also in step 5: the `--via` no-op arm of `ask_parse_args` is gone (commit de13cf2); `harness ask … --via x` is now an unknown option, exit 1.
+
+**Status.** Active. Supersedes the 4b consequence of [0005](0005-gate-only-inside-herdr.md). Gate 552 → 517 lines (the plan's ~420 was optimistic: most of the saving was already taken by the scanner and tables, and the path helpers stay).
+
+**Consequences.** Any new conductor shell command needs an allowlist entry and a gate test. The gate is a live symlink: edit via a new inode, `bash -n` plus `tests/gate.test.sh` before each save ([live-gate-edit](../troubleshooting/live-gate-edit.md)). A filesystem MCP server added later is not gated; add `mcp__filesystem` to `disallowedTools` then.
